ss"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "9262b6ac-540b-597f-88d5-5f11ae2e463c", "quiz": "e943634d-9fe6-514e-9002-fa5f24d890d1", "pos": 6, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nCompare how messages are sent in the nervous system and in the hormonal system.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": null, "model": "In the nervous system messages are electrical impulses along neurons [1]; in the hormonal system they are chemical hormones carried in the blood [1].", "points": [{"text": "In the nervous system messages are electrical impulses along neurons", "any": ["electrical", "impulse", "neuron"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "In the hormonal system they are chemical hormones carried in the blood", "any": ["chemical", "blood", "hormone"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "c41496ba-519e-5a48-9741-4f06b700f512", "quiz": "e943634d-9fe6-514e-9002-fa5f24d890d1", "pos": 7, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion D: Reflecting on the impacts of science]\nMobile phones distract drivers. Use your knowledge of stimulus and response to explain why using a phone while driving is dangerous, and suggest one rule that would help.", "options": [], "marks": 3, "section": "Criterion D", "correct": null, "model": "The brain is busy processing the phone conversation or screen, so it pays less attention to stimuli on the road [1]; the reaction time to a hazard is longer, so the car travels further before the driver brakes [1]; a law with fines for using a phone while driving would help [1].", "points": [{"text": "The brain is busy processing the phone conversation or screen, so it pays less attention to stimuli on the road", "any": ["attention", "distract", "brain", "process", "focus"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "The reaction time to a hazard is longer, so the car travels further before the driver brakes", "any": ["slower", "longer", "reaction", "delay", "late"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "A law with fines for using a phone while driving would help", "any": ["ban", "law", "fine", "hands-free", "switch off", "rule"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "5ddeb010-2f8a-5824-b476-1f119a802bc6", "quiz": "172e8391-8a35-55d7-b9ce-1f769138f2bd", "pos": 1, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nWhich part of a neuron?\nLong fibre that carries impulses away from the cell body", "options": ["Dendrite", "Axon", "Myelin sheath", "Cell body"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 1, "model": "Axon; cell body; myelin sheath; dendrite.", "points": null}, {"id": "901c8195-dd0f-561f-a5d0-5a0b689c727d", "quiz": "172e8391-8a35-55d7-b9ce-1f769138f2bd", "pos": 2, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nWhich part of a neuron?\nContains the nucleus", "options": ["Dendrite", "Axon", "Myelin sheath", "Cell body"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 3, "model": "Axon; cell body; myelin sheath; dendrite.", "points": null}, {"id": "5367a899-24c3-5da8-b7d9-64082cf0807d", "quiz": "172e8391-8a35-55d7-b9ce-1f769138f2bd", "pos": 3, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nWhich part of a neuron?\nInsulating layer that speeds up impulses", "options": ["Dendrite", "Axon", "Myelin sheath", "Cell body"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 2, "model": "Axon; cell body; myelin sheath; dendrite.", "points": null}, {"id": "4439aa52-80d7-5395-8de8-2815a0be8e12", "quiz": "172e8391-8a35-55d7-b9ce-1f769138f2bd", "pos": 4, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nWhich part of a neuron?\nReceives impulses from other neurons", "options": ["Dendrite", "Axon", "Myelin sheath", "Cell body"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 0, "model": "Axon; cell body; myelin sheath; dendrite.", "points": null}, {"id": "e680fc91-5e0f-5751-a23c-581ce1a4afb0", "quiz": "172e8391-8a35-55d7-b9ce-1f769138f2bd", "pos": 5, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nDescribe the functions of sensory, relay and motor neurons.", "options": [], "marks": 3, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": null, "model": "Sensory neurons carry impulses from receptors to the CNS [1]; relay neurons pass impulses within the CNS from sensory to motor neurons [1]; motor neurons carry impulses from the CNS to effectors such as muscles [1].", "points": [{"text": "Sensory neurons carry impulses from receptors to the CNS", "any": ["receptor to", "from receptors", "from a receptor"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Relay neurons pass impulses within the CNS from sensory to motor neurons", "any": ["within the cns", "inside the cns", "sensory to motor", "spinal cord"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Motor neurons carry impulses from the CNS to effectors such as muscles", "any": ["to effector", "to a muscle", "to muscles", "gland"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "a0febcaf-263d-5403-a2b9-0069c3dbf4c4", "quiz": "172e8391-8a35-55d7-b9ce-1f769138f2bd", "pos": 6, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nExplain the role of neurotransmitters at a synapse.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": null, "model": "Neurotransmitters are released by the first neuron and diffuse across the synaptic gap [1]; they bind to receptors on the next neuron and start a new impulse [1].", "points": [{"text": "Neurotransmitters are released by the first neuron and diffuse across the synaptic gap", "any": ["released", "diffuse", "cross the gap", "across the gap"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "They bind to receptors on the next neuron and start a new impulse", "any": ["bind", "receptor", "new impulse", "next neuron"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "08eca2e4-c39f-5161-9c57-25b273b2101f", "quiz": "172e8391-8a35-55d7-b9ce-1f769138f2bd", "pos": 7, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion C: Processing and evaluating]\nAn impulse travels 0.9 m along a myelinated axon in 0.010 s. Calculate its speed, and explain why the speed would be lower in an axon without myelin.", "options": [], "marks": 3, "section": "Criterion C", "correct": null, "model": "Speed = 0.9 ÷ 0.010 [1] = 90 m/s [1]; without the insulating myelin the impulse cannot jump along the axon, so it travels more slowly [1].", "points": [{"text": "Speed = 0.9 ÷ 0.010", "any": ["0.9 ÷ 0.010", "0.9/0.010", "0.9 / 0.01", "distance ÷ time", "distance / time"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "= 90 m/s", "any": ["90"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Without the insulating myelin the impulse cannot jump along the axon, so it travels more slowly", "any": ["insulat", "myelin speeds", "jump", "faster with myelin", "no insulation"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "66f71563-262b-531f-a8c2-1f63c0bdfbce", "quiz": "b38130b7-11f0-5d91-bdd6-fa9c9b02fc56", "pos": 1, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nDefine a reflex action and give one example.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": null, "model": "A fast, automatic (involuntary) response to a stimulus [1], for example blinking when something approaches the eye [1].", "points": [{"text": "A fast, automatic (involuntary) response to a stimulus", "any": ["automatic", "involuntary", "fast", "without thinking"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "For example blinking when something approaches the eye", "any": ["blink", "knee", "hot", "pupil", "cough", "sneeze", "withdraw"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "35dca6cd-9ab7-510a-8d65-6186c3b6b0c6", "quiz": "b38130b7-11f0-5d91-bdd6-fa9c9b02fc56", "pos": 2, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nDescribe the reflex arc that makes you blink when dust blows towards your eye.", "options": [], "marks": 4, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": null, "model": "Receptors in the eye detect the dust [1]; a sensory neuron carries the impulse to the CNS [1]; a relay neuron passes it on [1]; a motor neuron carries it to the eyelid muscles, which contract to blink [1].", "points": [{"text": "Receptors in the eye detect the dust", "any": ["receptor", "eye", "detect"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "A sensory neuron carries the impulse to the CNS", "any": ["sensory neuron", "sensory"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "A relay neuron passes it on", "any": ["relay", "cns", "brain stem", "spinal cord"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "A motor neuron carries it to the eyelid muscles, which contract to blink", "any": ["motor neuron", "muscle", "eyelid"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "03e7902c-f09c-5df8-a64f-0cb74216a251", "quiz": "b38130b7-11f0-5d91-bdd6-fa9c9b02fc56", "pos": 3, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion B: Inquiring and designing]\nPlan an investigation, using the ruler-drop test, to find out whether practice improves reaction time.", "options": [], "marks": 4, "section": "Criterion B", "correct": null, "model": "Independent variable: the number of practice attempts (e.g. day 1 to day 5) [1]; dependent variable: the distance the ruler falls, converted to reaction time [1]; control: the same hand, ruler, starting position and person dropping without warning [1]; repeat five times each session and calculate a mean [1].", "points": [{"text": "Independent variable: the number of practice attempts (e.g. day 1 to day 5)", "any": ["number of practice", "practice", "tries", "trials", "days"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Dependent variable: the distance the ruler falls, converted to reaction time", "any": ["distance", "cm", "reaction time"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Control: the same hand, ruler, starting position and person dropping without warning", "any": ["same hand", "same ruler", "same person", "same height", "same position", "no warning"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Repeat five times each session and calculate a mean", "any": ["repeat", "mean", "average", "more students"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "1179c4c8-7d70-5486-8e94-ff954c392fba", "quiz": "b38130b7-11f0-5d91-bdd6-fa9c9b02fc56", "pos": 4, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion C: Processing and evaluating]\nStudent A has a mean catch distance of 12 cm and student B 22 cm. Explain which student has the faster reaction time and suggest one reason for the difference.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion C", "correct": null, "model": "Student A, because the ruler fell a shorter distance, so less time passed before the catch [1]; A may practise sport or video games more, or B may be tired or distracted [1].", "points": [{"text": "Student A, because the ruler fell a shorter distance, so less time passed before the catch", "any": ["student a", "a has", "a is faster", "12"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "A may practise sport or video games more, or B may be tired or distracted", "any": ["practice", "tired", "sleep", "distract", "caffeine", "sport", "video games", "attention", "age"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "2bee40d9-6570-5de7-9d82-6f2af38c4c06", "quiz": "b51182d4-2f99-5715-affc-1e6b479f1a72", "pos": 1, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nName the bone.\nProtects the brain", "options": ["Skull", "Femur", "Humerus", "Ribs", "Vertebrae"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 0, "model": "Skull; femur; ribs; humerus; vertebrae.", "points": null}, {"id": "b883f378-48b1-5d6b-a257-d2fbdc4a8a80", "quiz": "b51182d4-2f99-5715-affc-1e6b479f1a72", "pos": 2, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nName the bone.\nThigh bone", "options": ["Skull", "Femur", "Humerus", "Ribs", "Vertebrae"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 1, "model": "Skull; femur; ribs; humerus; vertebrae.", "points": null}, {"id": "5bfebecf-3428-5ebd-913a-6d126618aed7", "quiz": "b51182d4-2f99-5715-affc-1e6b479f1a72", "pos": 3, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nName the bone.\nProtect the heart and lungs", "options": ["Skull", "Femur", "Humerus", "Ribs", "Vertebrae"], "marks": 1, "section": "Cri