same hand [1]; test many students, repeat three times each and compare the means [1].", "points": [{"text": "Measure grip strength with a dynamometer", "any": ["dynamometer", "grip", "measure"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "In students who play sport and those who do not, of the same age and sex, using the same hand", "any": ["same age", "same sex", "same hand", "same", "similar"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Test many students, repeat three times each and compare the means", "any": ["repeat", "many students", "large sample", "mean", "average", "compare"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "71527da9-3f66-5040-b920-63aa7b82692e", "quiz": "2f8487cc-6e9f-5219-8c7b-ba19ffc2ba9b", "pos": 4, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion D: Reflecting on the impacts of science]\nSuggest two choices a teenager could make to keep their musculoskeletal system healthy, and explain the evidence that each choice works.", "options": [], "marks": 4, "section": "Criterion D", "correct": null, "model": "Be active for at least 60 minutes a day [1], because exercise makes bones denser and muscles stronger [1]; carry a bag on both shoulders and sit with good posture (or eat calcium-rich food) [1], because this prevents back pain and strain on the spine (or calcium hardens bone) [1].", "points": [{"text": "Be active for at least 60 minutes a day", "any": ["exercise", "sport", "walk", "run", "active", "activity"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Because exercise makes bones denser and muscles stronger", "any": ["denser", "stronger", "flexible", "muscle", "bone"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Carry a bag on both shoulders and sit with good posture (or eat calcium-rich food)", "any": ["posture", "bag", "calcium", "diet", "screen", "sleep", "warm up", "milk"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Because this prevents back pain and strain on the spine (or calcium hardens bone)", "any": ["back pain", "strain", "bone", "harden", "injur", "spine", "healthy"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {