n: too hot.", "points": null}, {"id": "ee42e070-e259-5790-97ed-00f3e14fabd2", "quiz": "b9c8541a-0ae0-5d2e-8302-086d4ee6e2bb", "pos": 4, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nDoes this happen when the body is too hot or too cold?\nVasodilation", "options": ["Too hot", "Too cold"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 0, "model": "Vasoconstriction and shivering: too cold. Sweating and vasodilation: too hot.", "points": null}, {"id": "ac7e2472-b83d-5929-8f89-01847a55bcd9", "quiz": "b9c8541a-0ae0-5d2e-8302-086d4ee6e2bb", "pos": 5, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nName the part of the brain that controls body temperature and describe how it detects a change.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": null, "model": "The hypothalamus [1]; its receptors detect the temperature of the blood flowing through it (and receive impulses from thermoreceptors in the skin) [1].", "points": [{"text": "The hypothalamus", "any": ["hypothalamus"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Its receptors detect the temperature of the blood flowing through it (and receive impulses from thermoreceptors in the skin)", "any": ["receptor", "blood temperature", "thermoreceptor", "detects the temperature of the blood"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "a04f9843-0b3c-5823-bd87-072c6ab6f401", "quiz": "b9c8541a-0ae0-5d2e-8302-086d4ee6e2bb", "pos": 6, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nExplain how vasoconstriction reduces heat loss.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": null, "model": "The arterioles supplying the skin capillaries narrow [1], so less blood flows near the skin surface and less heat is lost by radiation [1].", "points": [{"text": "The arterioles supplying the skin capillaries narrow", "any": ["arterioles narrow", "narrow", "constrict"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Less blood flows near the skin surface and less heat is lost by radiation", "any": ["less blood", "surface", "less heat"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "2731222a-305d-52fc-abba-4bd2b998a6df", "quiz": "b9c8541a-0ae0-5d2e-8302-086d4ee6e2bb", "pos": 7, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion C: Processing and evaluating]\nA hiker's core temperature falls from 37.0 °C to 35.2 °C on a cold night on Mount Kenya. Calculate the fall, state the name of the condition when core temperature falls below 35 °C, and suggest why it is dangerous.", "options": [], "marks": 3, "section": "Criterion C", "correct": null, "model": "Fall = 37.0 − 35.2 = 1.8 °C [1]; below 35 °C the condition is hypothermia [1]; enzyme-controlled reactions slow down, so the heart and brain stop working properly, which can cause confusion and death [1].", "points": [{"text": "Fall = 37.0 − 35.2 = 1.8 °C", "any": ["1.8"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Below 35 °C the condition is hypothermia", "any": ["hypothermia"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Enzyme-controlled reactions slow down, so the heart and brain stop working properly, which can cause confusion and death", "any": ["enzyme", "slow", "reactions", "heart", "brain", "confus", "death", "die"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "00e64042-e665-5736-97ba-606337be52d7", "quiz": "b494a008-cbfb-5fa9-8550-44fa7a392b25", "pos": 1, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nName the organ or hormone.\nDetects blood glucose and releases hormones", "options": ["Pancreas", "Liver", "Insulin", "ADH", "Kidney"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 0, "model": "Pancreas; liver; insulin; ADH; kidney.", "points": null}, {"id": "ad18d576-66e3-5e41-87a5-ef5d2b240acb", "quiz": "b494a008-cbfb-5fa9-8550-44fa7a392b25", "pos": 2, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nName the organ or hormone.\nStores glucose as glycogen", "options": ["Pancreas", "Liver", "Insulin", "ADH", "Kidney"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 1, "model": "Pancreas; liver; insulin; ADH; kidney.", "points": null}, {"id": "45e75050-032f-59fc-bcfc-8d1ea2733362", "quiz": "b494a008-cbfb-5fa9-8550-44fa7a392b25", "pos": 3, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nName the organ or hormone.\nHormone that lowers blood glucose", "options": ["Pancreas", "Liver", "Insulin", "ADH", "Kidney"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 2, "model": "Pancreas; liver; insulin; ADH; kidney.", "points": null}, {"id": "267155db-0e50-506a-8187-76e07f9151df", "quiz": "b494a008-cbfb-5fa9-8550-44fa7a392b25", "pos": 4, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nName the organ or hormone.\nHormone that makes the kidneys reabsorb more water", "options": ["Pancreas", "Liver", "Insulin", "ADH", "Kidney"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 3, "model": "Pancreas; liver; insulin; ADH; kidney.", "points": null}, {"id": "d1932538-8da4-5875-b451-b728637aa4c3", "quiz": "b494a008-cbfb-5fa9-8550-44fa7a392b25", "pos": 5, "kind": "mcq", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nName the organ or hormone.\nOrgan that makes urine", "options": ["Pancreas", "Liver", "Insulin", "ADH", "Kidney"], "marks": 1, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": 4, "model": "Pancreas; liver; insulin; ADH; kidney.", "points": null}, {"id": "8054328b-b790-5fba-9f6f-8e643e3ca2b9", "quiz": "b494a008-cbfb-5fa9-8550-44fa7a392b25", "pos": 6, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion A: Knowing and understanding]\nExplain how the body responds when blood glucose falls during exercise.", "options": [], "marks": 3, "section": "Criterion A", "correct": null, "model": "The pancreas detects the fall [1] and releases glucagon [1]; glucagon makes the liver break down glycogen into glucose, raising blood glucose [1].", "points": [{"text": "The pancreas detects the fall", "any": ["pancreas", "detect"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Releases glucagon", "any": ["glucagon"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Glucagon makes the liver break down glycogen into glucose, raising blood glucose", "any": ["glycogen", "liver", "glucose released", "breaks down"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "d55529fe-1492-5839-9e1c-50f8608e7ded", "quiz": "b494a008-cbfb-5fa9-8550-44fa7a392b25", "pos": 7, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion C: Processing and evaluating]\nBlood glucose (mmol/L) of a person after a meal: 0 min 5.0; 30 min 8.5; 60 min 7.0; 90 min 5.5; 120 min 5.0. Calculate the maximum rise and the rate of fall between 30 and 90 minutes, and explain the fall.", "options": [], "marks": 4, "section": "Criterion C", "correct": null, "model": "Maximum rise = 8.5 − 5.0 = 3.5 mmol/L [1]; rate of fall = (8.5 − 5.5) ÷ 60 = 0.05 mmol/L per minute [1]; the pancreas released insulin [1], which made cells take up glucose and the liver store it as glycogen [1].", "points": [{"text": "Maximum rise = 8.5 − 5.0 = 3.5 mmol/L", "any": ["3.5"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Rate of fall = (8.5 − 5.5) ÷ 60 = 0.05 mmol/L per minute", "any": ["0.05"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "The pancreas released insulin", "any": ["insulin"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Which made cells take up glucose and the liver store it as glycogen", "any": ["glycogen", "cells take up", "take up glucose", "liver", "store"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}, {"id": "daa5e35d-6595-5948-9e0a-d3c575980f1f", "quiz": "b494a008-cbfb-5fa9-8550-44fa7a392b25", "pos": 8, "kind": "short", "prompt": "[Criterion D: Reflecting on the impacts of science]\nSuggest why many people in Kenya have type 2 diabetes without knowing it, and one way the health system could find them earlier.", "options": [], "marks": 2, "section": "Criterion D", "correct": null, "model": "The symptoms develop slowly and many people are never tested because clinics are far away or tests cost money [1]; free blood glucose screening by community health workers or at pharmacies would find them earlier [1].", "points": [{"text": "The symptoms develop slowly and many people are never tested because clinics are far away or tests cost money", "any": ["no symptoms", "mild", "slow", "not tested", "cost", "not aware", "clinic", "far", "gradual"], "all": [], "marks": 1}, {"text": "Free blood glucose screening by community health workers or at pharmacies would find them earlier", "any": ["screen", "test", "free", "community health", "pharmacy", "mobile", "campaign", "checks"], "all": [], "marks": 1}]}], "subject": "MYP Biology", "level": "Grade 9", "unit": "MYP 4 · Biology · Body systems", "first": 87, "cfirst": 14, "k": 18}$j$::jsonb; t uuid := (d->'topic'->>'id')::uuid; begin
  if (d->'topic'->>'new')::boolean then
    insert into public.topics (id, subject_id, programme, name, summary, sort_order, parent_id) select t, s.id, d->'topic'->>'programme', d->'topic'->>'name', d->'topic'->>'summary', (d->'topic'->>'sort')::int, (d->'topic'->>'parent')::uuid
      from public.subjects s where s.name = 'MYP Science' on conflict (id) do nothing;
  end if;
  insert into public.lessons (id, topic_id, title, summary, url, external_id, max_marks, sort_order) select (l->>'id')::uuid, t, l->>'title', l->>'summary', l->>'url', l->>'ext', (l->>'max')::int, (l->>'sort')::int from jsonb_array_elements(d->'lessons') l
    on conflict (external_id) do update set title = excluded.title, url = excluded.url, max_marks = excluded.max_marks, topic_id = excluded.topic_id, sort_order = excluded.sort_order;
  insert into public.lesson_specs (lesson, title, spec, updated_at) select l->>'ext', l->>'title', l->'spec', now() from jsonb_array_elements(d->'lessons') l
    on conflict (lesson) do update set title = excluded.title, spec = excluded.spec, updated_at = now();
  if not exists (select 1 from public.materials m join jsonb_array_elements(d->'lessons') l on m.path = l->>'url') then   -- make room once: everything after the anchor moves down
    update public.materials set sort = sort + (d->>'k')::int where sort >= (d->>'first')::int;
    update public.class_materials cm set sort = cm.sort + (d->>'k')::int where cm.sort >= (d->>'cfirst')::int and cm.class_id in (select a.class_id from public.class_materials a where a.path = d->>'anchor');
  end if;
  insert into public.materials (path, lesson_id, title, kind, subject, level, unit, sort) select l->>'url', l->>'ext', l->>'title', 'lesson', d->>'subject', d->>'level', d->>'unit', (l->>'msort')::int from jsonb_array_elements(d->'lessons') l
    on conflict (path) do update set lesson_id = excluded.lesson_id, title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, subject = excluded.subject, level = excluded.level, unit = excluded.unit, sort = excluded.sort;
  insert into public.class_materials (class_id, path, sort) select a.class_id, l->>'url', (l->>'csort')::int from jsonb_array_elements(d->'lessons') l join public.class_materials a on a.path = d->>'anchor' on conflict do nothing;
  insert into public.quizzes (id, topic_id, title, instructions, time_limit_minutes, max_attempts, published, show_results, category, feedback_mode, created_by)
    select (q->>'id')::uuid, t, q->>'title', q->>'instr', null, 2, true, true, 'quiz', 'hybrid', 'a9774d11-5d83-4bae-8da1-a6fb81c7dd7e' from jsonb_array_elements(d->'quizzes') q
    on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, instructions = excluded.instructions, topic_id = excluded.topic_id;
  if exists (select 1 from information_schema.columns where table_schema = 'public' and table_name = 'quizzes' and column_name = 'subject') then
    update public.quizzes set subject = 'Biology' where id in (select (q->>'id')::uuid from jsonb_array_elements(d->'quizzes') q);
  end if;
  insert into public.questions (id, topic_id, kind, prompt, options, marks, section, created_by) select (q->>'id')::uuid, t, q->>'kind', q->>'prompt', q->'options', (q->>'marks')::int, q->>'section', 'a9774d11-5d83-4bae-8da1-a6fb81c7dd7e' from jsonb_array_elements(d->'questions') q
    on conflict (id) do update set prompt = excluded.prompt, options = excluded.options, marks = excluded.marks, kind = excluded.kind, section = excluded.section;
  insert into public.question_answers (question_id, correct_option, model_answer, mark_scheme, points, explanation)
    select (q->>'id')::uuid, (q->>'correct')::int, case when q->>'kind' = 'mcq' then q->'options'->>((q->>'correct')::int) else q->>'model' end, case when q->>'kind' = 'mcq' then null else q->>'model' end,
           case when q->>'kind' = 'mcq' then null else q->'points' end, q->>'model' from jsonb_array_elements(d->'questions') q
    on conflict (question_id) do update set correct_option = excluded.correct_option, model_answer = excluded.model_answer, mark_scheme = excluded.mark_scheme, points = excluded.points, explanation = excluded.explanation;
  insert into public.quiz_questions (quiz_id, question_id, position) select (q->>'quiz')::uuid, (q->>'id')::uuid, (q->>'pos')::int from jsonb_array_elements(d->'questions') q
    on conflict (quiz_id, question_id) do update set position = excluded.position;
  insert into public.quiz_classes (quiz_id, class_id, published, published_at, published_by)
    select (q->>'id')::uuid, c.id, c.teacher_id = 'a9774d11-5d83-4bae-8da1-a6fb81c7dd7e', case when c.teacher_id = 'a9774d11-5d83-4bae-8da1-a6fb81c7dd7e' then now() end, case when c.teacher_id = 'a9774d11-5d83-4bae-8da1-a6fb81c7dd7e' then 'a9774d11-5d83-4bae-8da1-a6fb81c7dd7e'::uuid end
      from jsonb_array_elements(d->'quizzes') q cross join public.classes c where c.id in (select a.class_id from public.class_materials a where a.path = d->>'anchor')
    on conflict do nothing;
end $do$;
select (select count(*) from public.lessons where external_id like 'G9-BIO-BODY-L%') as lessons, (select count(*) from public.lesson_specs where lesson like 'G9-BIO-BODY-L%') as specs, (select count(*) from public.materials where path like '/g9-bio-body-%') as materials, (select count(*) from public.class_materials where path like '/g9-bio-body-%') as class_links, (select count(*) from public.quizzes where topic_id = '004396a5-19db-5ac6-9df6-126e61518dca' and title like '%exam-style questions') as exam_sets, (select count(*) from public.quiz_questions qq join public.quizzes q on q.id = qq.quiz_id where q.topic_id = '004396a5-19db-5ac6-9df6-126e61518dca' and q.title like '%exam-style questions') as exam_questions;
